{title: Palti Son of Rafu}
{subtitle: Numbers 13:2–9; 13:17–21; 13:25–33; 14:1–29}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 86}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | ×17

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
From the tribe of Benjamin, Palti son of Rafu
Sent by Mo[Cm]ses from the Wilderness of Paran
[Eb]One leader chosen from each ancestral line
[Ab]To scout the land of Ca[Bb]naan, di[Ab]vine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
See what the [Bb]land is like, strong [Eb]or weak
Are their [Ab]towns open [Bb]camps or fortified [Eb]peaks
Is the soil rich or poor, trees on it or [Ab]not
Be bold and bring back [Bb]the fruit, the lot
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Cm]They went up from Zin [Bb]as far as Re[Eb]hob
Neared Le-bo-ha-[Ab]math, tested the [Eb]path
[Cm]Forty days they [Ab]traveled through the [Eb]land
[Cm]Then returned to [Ab]the people, in the [Bb]hand
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
See what [Ab]the land is [Bb]like, strong or weak
[Eb]Are their towns o[Ab]pen camps or [Bb]fortified peaks
Is [Eb]the soil rich or poor, trees on it or not
Be [Ab]bold and bring back the fruit, [Bb]the lot
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
It tru[Cm]ly does flow with milk [Bb]and honey [Eb]
But the people [Ab]are strong, cities [Eb]are large
We [Cm]saw the de[Ab]scendants of Anak [Eb]there
[Cm]Amalekites [Ab]in the Ne[Bb]gev, the air
[Ab]Hittites and Je[Bb]busites in the [Eb]hills
[Ab]Canaanites [Bb]by the sea and the [Cm]fields
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Ab]Caleb qui[Bb]eted the people [Eb]be[Ab]fore Moses
Said we should [Bb]go up and take pos[Eb]session
[Ab]But the others [Bb]said we cannot at[Eb]tack
They are [Ab]stronger than we are, [Bb]weak and lack
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
See what [Cm]the land is [Ab]like, strong or weak
Are [Bb]their towns o[Eb]pen camps or for[Ab]tified peaks
[Bb]Is the soil rich or [Eb]poor, trees on it or not
Be bold and bring back [Ab]the fruit, the lot
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
In our [Bb]eyes we seemed like [Cm]grasshop[Bb]pers
So [Eb]we seemed to them, [Ab]the shadow [Eb]of copers
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
